& =(20)^2+(24)^2-(20)^2-(56)^2 \\
& =(24)^2-(56)^2=576-3136 \\
& =-2560=-2.56 \mathrm{~kJ}
\end{aligned}

Hence, change in potential energy of the ball after $t=85 \mathrm{~s}$ is $-2.56 \mathrm{KJ}$.
